
# The server DOM's view handle: a `page-element`, the in-memory record `./dom` builds. Typed here so a read through the
# handle (`node/handle/children`) is a read of a list, and the seam on by default has nothing to refuse. The other
# backends define their own `view` beside this one (../memory/view, ../browser/view, ../toolkit/view, ../view), and the
# build bears the one for its target through ../../view.

load @term/base/list
  find list

load @term/base/maybe
  find maybe

form view
  link handle, like page-element, mark private

# one node of the tree, held by its parent's children list and by every view handle at once, so `note shared`
form page-element
  mark shared
  link tag, like text
  link text, like text
  link value, like text
  link attributes, like list
  link styles, like list
  link classes, like list
  link children, like list
  link listeners, like list
  link parent
    like maybe
      like view
